      "content": "Certainly! Here is your justification:\n\nQuantum entanglement and non-locality are pivotal concepts in quantum mechanics that underpin modern quantum computing. Quantified by peculiar correlations between entangled particles, this principle is the bedrock for advancements in communications, cryptography, and computational capacities. My research on quantum entanglement and non-locality seeks to delve deeper into understanding Bell inequalities, which are fundamental to verifying non-locality.\n\nEntanglement plays a crucial role in improving robustness against decoherence, a primary hurdle in maintaining quantum states during computations. By addressing entanglement-decoherence interplay, my work aspires to enhance the fidelity of qubit states, a critical pathway to scaling up quantum computers. Furthermore, my study will integrate entanglement-swapping protocols, potentially opening innovative avenues for enhancing quantum information transmission.\n\nThis research holds the promise of revolutionizing both quantum computing and our understanding of quantum mechanics, positioning it as an essential endeavor within the Horizon Europe framework. Emphasizing quantum-state manipulation and entanglement dynamics, it aligns perfectly with the thematic priorities of fostering quantum technologies predicated on foundational principles.\n\nI believe my research will provide significant strides towards the realization of scalable, fault-tolerant quantum computing, contributing profoundly to both theoretical and applied",
